igens  using the same stimulation conditions in  an immune cell killing assay  the graph on the right shows that target  cell death aligns temporally with the  cd8 proliferation data  which suggests the enrichment of the cd8  subpopulation  serves to attack and kill any target  cells present  this film on the far right shows cd8  labelled cells  interacting with satellite labeled  sculp3 cells  which are a cancer cell line once the  cd8 cells  have detected the target cell the t cell  then creates an immunological synapse  between the two cells  using the poor forming protein perforin  this then allows it to pump  apoptosis-inducing proteins  into the target cell in order to induce  death  this example shows how incusi technology  can be used to identify and monitor  change in a specific sub-population  and then link this to a functional  output so in conclusion  incusite cell by cell analysis provides  an integrated solution for identifying  and quantifying subsets of living cells  in heterogeneous cultures over time the  module  enables temporal analysis of cell  subsets based on morphology  biomarkers health and function the assay  setup does not require cell lifting  fixing or staining and the simple  experimental analysis workflows are  amenable to the everyday user  this module provides a further dimension  to lifestyle analysis  for non-adherent cells where the user  may answer biological questions at the  cell by cell level
 

